    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP on this May 22nd, **Corbin Carroll** stands as the definitive anchor of our lineup. With an elite score of 85.94, he benefits from a succulent matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano (xERA 4.80) and a significant boost from a slow pitcher delivery, which elevates his stolen base potential\u2014the lifeblood of our strategy. Joining him in the \"Strong\" tier are **Tyler Soderstrom** (69.05) and **Seiya Suzuki** (66.75). **Seiya Suzuki** particularly intrigues; despite a \"Wind In\" penalty, his favorable platoon advantage against Arrighetti and a generous park factor keep him well above our 60-point start threshold. Meanwhile, **James Wood** is a priority play at the utility spot; leading off against Elder provides him a path to volume and run-scoring that pushes his score to 65.47, aided by high underlying xwOBA metrics.\n\nThe most difficult decision at the margins involved **Kyle Karros**, who landed on the bench with a 43.54 score. While he cleared our \"Below Floor\" threshold, he was ultimately squeezed out by the sheer depth of our starting group, particularly with **Mickey Moniak** (65.70) drawing a favorable start against Michael Soroka. **Mickey Moniak** projects to hit second, providing him the best opportunity to maximize his sprint speed and platoon advantage. We remain cautious with **Vinnie Pasquantino** (53.20) and **Brice Turang** (52.01); while their scores are respectable, they face stiffer opposition from Gilbert and Wrobleski, respectively. Investors should monitor the official lineup cards for **Gabriel Moreno**, **Corbin Carroll**, and **Mickey Moniak** closely, as any shift down the batting order would necessitate a recalibration of their efficiency scores.",
